# Only what this project actually produces. The generated file libGDX ships covers android, ios,
# html, gwt, teavm, robovm, netbeans and lwjgl2, none of which exist here, and it listed build
# directories one module at a time - which is how `map/` came to be missing from it. The build and
# bin rules below match at any depth instead, so adding a module never means editing this file.

## Build output
build/
/dist/
bin/
.gradle/
gradle-app.setting
local.properties

## Java
*.class
*.war
*.ear
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*
.attach_pid*

## IntelliJ
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

## Eclipse
.classpath
.project
